  "reason": "Format 2 records, beside the SHA-256 the index was proved with, the content's CRC32C and the file's modification time, file key and creation time at that moment. An ordinary file is keyed by path, size and file key instead of every attribute, so a touched file still finds its index. Reuse follows the maintainer's decision of 2026-10-21: unchanged attributes that the file system vouches for are trusted without reading the file; a moved modification time, or attributes without a file key or sub-second time, are checked by CRC32C; anything else takes the SHA-256 proof and a new scan. Format-1 indexes lack the recorded proof and are refused by version and removed by the startup sweep; the scan recipe and the decoded facts are unchanged.",
